Craig,

I found the old Fortran program I wrote in 1967 to test the Markowitz  
method.
Actually, I used Fortran 2.1, which was the new release at the time.

See attached program.  The maximum number of stocks that the IBM
mainframe could handle was 52x52 -- that was a brand new mainframe
at OSU that I was able to use in July-August, 1967.

I'll send you a copy of the paper I wrote in late 1966, describing how  
the
Markowitz method works,  It reads like it is over 40 years old --  
which it is.
You'll get a kick out of some of the statements in the paper.

Dad
++++++++++++++++++++

